Comment 	=> 'Area-weighted average of all rice irrigated crops available water capacity, from the MIRCA crop dataset.  There are 3 rice rice crops in the MIRCA dataset.  awCap is calculated by: root depth x (field capacity - wilting point).  Crop root depths are from Siebert S and Doll P, 2010, Quanitifying blue and green virtual water contentents in global crop production as well as potential production losses without irrigation. Journal of Hydrology, 384, 198-217. Field capacity and wilting point are from the UNESCO/FAO soil map of the world (FAO/UNESCO, 2003. Digital Soil Map of the World and Derived Soil Properties Version 3.6. CD ROM.',
